From: baseband lane
Subject: 0522 pandora_mpss: optionally shut the peripheral down before the first INIT_IMAGE

The ladder shuts the modem down at step 5, which is AFTER step 4 has already made its first
INIT_IMAGE call.  But the modem is whatever the previous boot left it when this kernel starts:
Android boots the modem on every start, and a warm reset does not necessarily leave it in reset.

If the secure world requires a peripheral to be in reset before it accepts a fresh image, then every
INIT_IMAGE from this ladder would be refused regardless of how correct the id, the metadata, the
bridge and the DSM assignment are -- and every one of those has now been checked against upstream or
against the firmware bytes.

pandora_mpss_shutdown_first=1 now issues PAS_SHUTDOWN for the main id and the DTB id at the top of
step 4, before anything else.  PAS_SHUTDOWN on an id that is not running is harmless.

Off by default, so it can be crossed with the other experiments in one diagnostic boot:

    pandora_mpss_step=4 pandora_mpss_shutdown_first=1 pandora_mpss_assign=1

diff --git a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c b/b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
index a269ff3..53eb080 100755
--- a/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
+++ b/bsd/dev/pandora_mpss.c
@@ -935,9 +935,35 @@ mp_probe_cross(void)
 	}
 }
 
+/*
+ * Put the peripheral back into reset before asking TrustZone anything.
+ *
+ * The ladder shuts the modem down at step 5, i.e. AFTER step 4's first INIT_IMAGE.  But when this
+ * kernel starts, the modem is whatever the previous boot left it: Android boots the modem on every
+ * start, and a warm reset does not necessarily clear it.  If the secure world insists that a
+ * peripheral be in reset before it will accept a fresh image, every INIT_IMAGE from here would be
+ * refused no matter how correct the metadata or the bridge is.
+ *
+ * Off by default; pandora_mpss_shutdown_first=1 enables it.  PAS_SHUTDOWN on an id that is not
+ * running is harmless (it answers something other than 0 and nothing else changes).
+ */
+static void
+mp_shutdown_first(void)
+{
+	static const unsigned ids[] = { MP_PAS, MP_PAS_DTB };
+
+	if (!mp_option("pandora_mpss_shutdown_first")) {
+		return;
+	}
+	for (unsigned i = 0; i < sizeof(ids) / sizeof(ids[0]); i++) {
+		(void)pandora_pas_shutdown(ids[i]);
+	}
+}
+
 static bool
 step_dtb(void)
 {
+	mp_shutdown_first();
 	mp_probe_pas_ids();
 	mp_probe_cross();
 	if (!mp_assign_dsm()) {
